    <sectiondef kind="user-defined">
      <header>Copy and move special members</header>
      <description><para>Trivial copy and move because <ref refid="classEnvLoader" kindref="compound">EnvLoader</ref> owns no state of its own.</para>
<para><ref refid="classEnvLoader" kindref="compound">EnvLoader</ref> has no data members: the only state it touches is the stateless, process-wide environment reached through the inherited <ref refid="classEnvVars" kindref="compound">EnvVars</ref> helpers. The compiler-generated copy/move constructors and assignment operators are therefore correct, and spelling them out with <computeroutput>= default</computeroutput> makes that intent explicit. Derived sections own their own settings, so each of them controls its own copy and move behaviour. </para>
</description>
