    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="classBase" kindref="compound">Base</ref> for configuration sections that read typed values from the process environment. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Extends <ref refid="classEnvVars" kindref="compound">EnvVars</ref> with a family of <ref refid="classEnvLoader_1a3433869e7d95286c2dcf0360cd9c06eb" kindref="member">getEnvironmentVariable()</ref> overloads that convert a raw string into the target type and fall back to a caller-supplied default when the variable is absent (or, for numeric/duration types, malformed). Conversion failures are reported through <ref refid="classMessage_1a1fd9a043b58e6adceb8d111bc891feba" kindref="member">Message::ErrorMessage</ref> rather than thrown, so a bad environment cannot prevent startup. Derived classes must implement <ref refid="classEnvLoader_1a4f95654bec2fd3765dd4d725e0581d9f" kindref="member">printValues()</ref> and typically call these accessors from their constructor initializer lists.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>Numeric overloads parse through std::stoi, so integer values outside the range of a signed int are rejected even when the destination type is wider. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para>A present boolean variable equals true only when it is exactly &quot;true&quot;; any other present value is interpreted as false (not as the supplied default). </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classEnvVars" kindref="compound">EnvVars</ref>, <ref refid="classConfigurator" kindref="compound">Configurator</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
